<h1>height</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
The maximum distance of any <a href="node.html"><em>node</em></a> from the <a href="root.html"><em>root</em></a>. If a tree has only one node (the root), the height is zero.   The height of an empty tree is not defined.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="depth.html"><em>depth</em></a>, <a href="level.html"><em>level</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
An equivalent definition is: the height is the maximum <a href="depth.html"><em>depth</em></a> of any node. </p> 
<p> The height of the figure at the definition of <a href="tree.html"><em>tree</em></a> is two. </p> 
<p> The height of a tree is also known as the <a href="order.html"><em>order</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

